$ factory work enqueue -h
exit 0
--- stdout
usage: factory work enqueue [flags]

Enqueue one work item by value: --title and the other flags, or --file with
the JSON body POST /api/v1/work takes (docs/api.md). Enqueueing an item that
exists, by --source and --external-id or by --idempotency-key, returns it and
creates nothing. Enqueueing by tracker URL waits on the input adapters (#7, #18).

Flags:
  --blocked-by ITEMS
      comma-separated items (IDs or source:external_id) that must finish first
  --body STRING
      the item's description, the brief an agent works from
  --external-id ID
      the item's ID in its source, such as autobutler-org/quark#123
  --external-url URL
      the item's URL in its source
  --file FILE
      read the item from this JSON file; - reads stdin. No other item flag may
      be given with it
  --idempotency-key KEY
      a key for work with no source: a repeat with the same key creates
      nothing
  --output FORMAT
      output format: table or json (default table)
  --priority INT
      higher is handed out first
  --repos REPOSITORIES
      comma-separated repositories (owner/name) the work changes
  --requires CAPABILITIES
      comma-separated capabilities a worker needs, such as claude
  --server URL
      the factory server's URL, such as http://127.0.0.1:8080 (default
      $FACTORY_SERVER)
  --source STRING
      the tracker the item comes from, such as github
  --state STRING
      design or ready (the server's default is ready)
  --title TITLE
      the item's title (required without --file)

Environment:
  FACTORY_SERVER       the server's URL when --server is not given
  FACTORY_API_TOKEN    the API token the server was started with
--- stderr
